  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'What is electroplating? (3 marks)', 'Electroplating is the process of coating an object with a thin layer of a metal by electrolysis.
The object to be plated is made the cathode (negative electrode), the plating metal is made the anode, and the electrolyte is a solution of a salt of the plating metal (e.g. silver nitrate or nickel sulphate). When current passes, metal ions in the solution are reduced and deposited on the object, while the anode dissolves to replace them.
It is used to prevent corrosion and improve appearance or hardness, e.g. chromium or nickel plating of taps, bicycle parts and surgical instruments, silver and gold plating of jewellery and utensils, and tin plating of food cans.', null, '[{"point": "Electroplating: depositing a thin layer of one metal on another object by electrolysis", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Method: object to be plated is the cathode, plating metal is the anode, electrolyte is a solution of a salt of the plating metal; metal ions are reduced and deposited on the cathode", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Purposes/examples: prevent corrosion, improve appearance/hardness - chromium or nickel plating of taps and surgical instruments, silver/gold plating of jewellery, tin plating of cans", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'medical-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
