  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Define health as per the World Health Organization (WHO) definition, and explain the dimensions of health. (3 marks)', 'According to the WHO constitution (1948): "Health is a state of complete physical, mental and social well-being and not merely the absence of disease or infirmity."
This means health is a positive state with several dimensions:
• Physical - the body and its organs function properly; good fitness, nutrition and sleep.
• Mental - emotional and psychological well-being; the ability to cope with stress, think clearly and work productively.
• Social - good relationships with family and community and the ability to fit into society.
Spiritual and emotional dimensions are also recognised, which match Bhutan''s idea of well-being under Gross National Happiness.', null, '[{"point": "WHO (1948): ''Health is a state of complete physical, mental and social well-being and not merely the absence of disease or infirmity''", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Physical dimension (body functioning, fitness), mental dimension (emotional/psychological well-being), social dimension (relationships, community)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Other dimensions often added: spiritual, emotional; linked to Bhutan''s Gross National Happiness/well-being", "marks": 0.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
