  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Define diffusion and give two examples of diffusion in the human body. (3 marks)', 'Diffusion is the net movement of molecules or ions from a region where they are in higher concentration to a region of lower concentration, down a concentration gradient, until they are evenly distributed. It is a passive process that needs no energy; its rate increases with temperature, a steeper gradient and a larger, thinner surface.
Examples in the body: (1) gas exchange in the lungs - oxygen diffuses from the alveoli into the blood and carbon dioxide from the blood into the alveoli; (2) oxygen and glucose diffuse from blood capillaries into tissue cells, while carbon dioxide and urea diffuse out; some products of digestion are absorbed in the small intestine by diffusion.', null, '[{"point": "Diffusion: net movement of molecules/ions from a region of higher concentration to lower concentration (down a concentration gradient) until evenly distributed; passive, no energy needed", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Example 1: oxygen from alveoli into blood and CO₂ from blood into alveoli", "marks": 0.75}, {"point": "Example 2: oxygen/glucose from capillaries into tissue cells, or absorption of some digested food in the intestine", "marks": 0.75}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'medical-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
